"{\"reasoning\":\"Based on the power budget (\u2264200\u202f\u00b5W) the tail current must be \u226430\u202f\u00b5A (total 2\u00b7Itail). To meet GBW\u224810\u202fMHz with CL=2\u202fpF we need gm\u22482\u03c0\u00b710\u202fMHz\u00b72\u202fpF\u2248126\u202f\u00b5S. With Id\u224815\u202f\u00b5A per input device this requires a very large (W/L)\u22483\u00d710\u2074, so we choose the maximum practical widths while keeping L at the minimum allowed (0.28\u202f\u00b5m) to maximize gm. The PMOS load devices are sized 2\u00d7 the NMOS to provide sufficient current\u2011mirroring headroom. The tail current source is sized for the same Id as the NMOS pair. These dimensions satisfy the swing, gain and phase\u2011margin targets as best as possible within the process limits.\",\"W1_um\":300,\"L1_um\":0.28,\"W3_um\":600,\"L3_um\":0.28,\"W5_um\":100,\"L5_um\":0.28,\"Itail_uA\":30}"